{% comment %}
  Which photos belong to a color.

  Photos are uploaded one color at a time — every photo of the first color,
  then every photo of the next — and each color's sizes are linked to the FIRST
  photo of that color's run (the WMS Images tab "colour:" pick, or "variant
  image" in Shopify admin). So a color's set runs from its linked photo up to,
  not including, the next photo that is linked to any variant.

  Outputs the media ids of that set for `variant`, comma-separated, in upload
  order. Outputs nothing when the variant has no linked photo.

  Sets need at least two different linked photos. With one (a single color, or
  every color pointing at the same photo) the product has one set of photos,
  not one per color, so the set is just the linked photo — exactly what the
  theme did before: that photo first, the rest in upload order.

  main-product.liquid renders this set first, so a page that opens on the
  second color (first color sold out, or a link to that color) shows that
  color's photos on top. carbon-color-gallery does the same live when the
  shopper changes color.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cs_featured = variant.featured_media
  if cs_featured != null
    assign cs_starts = product.images | where: 'attached_to_variant?', true | map: 'src'
    assign cs_in = false
    if cs_starts.size < 2
      echo cs_featured.id | append: ','
    else
      for cs_media in product.media
        if cs_media.id == cs_featured.id
          assign cs_in = true
        elsif cs_in and cs_starts contains cs_media.src
          break
        endif
        if cs_in
          echo cs_media.id | append: ','
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif
-%}
